### Independent-source comparison and identity resolution

- Anthropic's official Sonnet history lists Sonnet 5.5, Sonnet 5, Sonnet 4.6, Sonnet 4.5, Sonnet 4, and Sonnet 3.7; Sonnet 5.4 is absent ([Anthropic Sonnet page](https://www.anthropic.com/claude/sonnet)). The current first-party model overview likewise lists Sonnet 5.5 and Sonnet 5, with no 5.4 entry ([Claude Platform models overview](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/about-claude/models/overview)).
- Anthropic's release notes record the Sonnet 5.5 launch on 2026-09-28 and describe it as a successor to Sonnet 5, with no intervening 5.4 launch ([Claude Platform release notes](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/release-notes/overview)). The current and recently retired model table likewise contains no Sonnet 5.4 lifecycle entry ([model deprecations](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/about-claude/model-deprecations)).
- Anthropic's versioning documentation explains that dateless major-release IDs such as `claude-sonnet-5` omit the minor segment, while the later point release uses `claude-sonnet-5-5`; it provides no `5-4` example ([model IDs and versioning](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/about-claude/models/model-ids-and-versions)).
- Live independent catalogs agree with the first-party record: OpenRouter exposes `anthropic/claude-sonnet-5` and `anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5` but no Sonnet 5.4 ([OpenRouter models API](https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/models)); models.dev's provider catalog contains Sonnet 5 and 5.5 routes but no exact 5.4 ID ([models.dev API](https://models.dev/api.json)); and OpenCode Zen's live catalog contains `claude-sonnet-5` and `claude-sonnet-5-5` but no `claude-sonnet-5-4` ([OpenCode Zen models](https://opencode.ai/zen/v1/models)).
- Multiple searches using the exact display name and possible API spellings returned only generic Claude pages and the real Sonnet 5/5.5 records, not an exact 5.4 model card, system card, announcement, benchmark, or review. This creates a conflict with the repository label but not with the public vendor record: the likely explanations are a conflation of Sonnet 5 with 5.5, an internal/preview label, or a phantom entry.
- Because no exact model or benchmark was verified, Sonnet 5 and 5.5 measurements were deliberately not merged into this record. No normalized score is defensible without evidence for the exact ID.

